Spec: Project/Dependencies

Purpose:
  Define the generic dependency relationships between SDDRA ecosystem
  modules. This is the project-level instance — not a reusable schema.

Owns:
  Module dependency graph
  Cross-module contract definitions
  Dependency rules for the SDDRA ecosystem

RelationTypes:
  depends_on
  produces
  consumes
  calls
  owns
  tested_by
  deployed_by

DependencyGraph:

  gamification-module:
    depends_on:
      - database (persistence)
      - external-api (third-party gamification service)
      - cache (sorted sets, rate limits)
      - message-broker (async event processing)
    does_not_depend_on:
      - credit-module

  integration-module:
    depends_on:
      - database (primary storage)
      - cache (session, rate limiting)
      - message-broker (async messaging)
      - http-client (external API calls)
    does_not_depend_on:
      - gamification-module

  matchmaking-module:
    depends_on:
      - database (durable config)
      - cache (queues, sessions, locks)
      - orm (data access)
    does_not_depend_on:
      - gamification-module
      - credit-module

CrossModuleContracts:

  gamification-field-mapping:
    purpose: Field mapping between internal gamification events and external API
    owned_by: gamification-module + integration-module
    contract:
      - internal_event_type -> external_event_type mapping
      - field_path for nested payloads
      - transformation_rules for data normalization
      - static_field support for fixed API parameters

  gamification-audit-log:
    purpose: Audit trail for all gamification actions
    owned_by: gamification-module + integration-module
    contract:
      - correlation_id (links to point event, badge event)
      - user_id / external_id
      - action_type (POINT_AWARD, BADGE_UNLOCK, RANK_CHANGE)
      - request_data / response_data
      - execution_time_ms
      - is_successful flag
      - rollback_reference (if applicable)

  gamification-event-pattern:
    purpose: Common event processing pattern for gamification actions
    owned_by: gamification-module + event-processor
    contract:
      - event claiming (idempotent lock by event_id)
      - handler dispatch (action_type -> processor)
      - rule evaluation (gamification rules engine)
      - batch completion
      - retry with count tracking
      - dead-letter queue for failed events

  player-identity-mapping:
    purpose: Bidirectional mapping between internal user ID and external platform ID
    owned_by: gamification-module + user-service
    contract:
      - internal_user_id <-> external_id mapping
      - provider identifier
      - status (active, merged, deprecated)
      - TTL-based cache invalidation
      - merge support for user migration

  shared-field-mapping:
    purpose: Common field mapping engine used by Integration domain
    owned_by: integration-module + gamification-module
    contract:
      - internal_field -> external_field mapping
      - field_path (dot notation for nested objects)
      - transformation_rules (uppercase, digits_only, remove_plus)
      - static_field support with default_value

  shared-http-client:
    purpose: HTTP client abstraction for external API calls
    owned_by: integration-module + gamification-module
    contract:
      - content-type handling (json, form-data, form-urlencoded)
      - auth header injection
      - timeout and retry configuration
      - standardized response format (status_code, response_body, success)

  shared-audit-log:
    purpose: Integration request/response audit trail
    owned_by: integration-module + gamification-module
    contract:
      - request_id (correlation ID)
      - integration_id / target_service
      - request_body / request_data
      - response_body / response_data
      - execution_time_ms
      - is_successful flag

Rules:
  [DEP1] Dependencies MUST have an explicit owner.
  [DEP2] Circular dependencies MUST be detectable and prohibited.
  [DEP3] New dependencies MUST be evaluated against architecture principles (AP1-AP18).
  [DEP4] Cross-module contracts MUST be explicitly declared and versioned.
  [DEP5] A module MUST NOT depend on another module's internal structures.
  [DEP6] Shared kernel contracts MUST be reviewed by all owning modules before change.
  [DEP7] Dependency changes MUST be recorded in decisions/rules.sdd.

Navigation:
  Domains: @../project/domains.sdd
  Modules: @../project/modules.sdd
  Flows: @../project/flows.sdd
  Architecture: @../../architecture/principles.sdd

State: +